# Keeps the Docker build context small and avoids leaking local-only files into an image.
# Nested bin/obj (any depth) matter most: a copied-in obj/project.assets.json from a Windows host
# `dotnet build` references Windows-only NuGet fallback folders (e.g. "C:\Program Files (x86)\...
# \NuGetPackages") and breaks `dotnet publish` inside the Linux build stage - so these must be
# excluded at every depth, not just the repo root.
**/bin/
**/obj/
.vs/
*.user

node_modules/
webapp/dist/

# Never bake local secrets into an image - config is injected via env vars at runtime instead.
appsettings.Development.json
webapp/.env.local

.git/
